# Scenario: is a prepared mound still chosen as an exit?
#
# Reported from play: a molehill shored up with loose soil stopped being
# travelled to. Moles stood seven blocks away and ignored it while working
# other mounds in the same colony.
#
# The selection path reads as block-agnostic - MoundNetwork.chooseExit filters
# on colony membership, distance and isPositionEntityTicking, nothing else, and
# the mounds come from a point-of-interest query whose type covers both blocks.
# So either the reading is wrong or the point of interest does not survive the
# block being replaced. This decides it.
#
# The fixture is symmetric on purpose. Two mounds, same distance from the mole,
# same everything except that one is shored up. Over an hour of game time a
# fair chooser hits both. If the log names only one, the difference is the block.
#
#   SEARCH_RADIUS 16   - both mounds must be inside it to be scanned at all
#   MIN_EXIT_DISTANCE 12 - and outside it, or neither can serve as an exit
#
# 14 satisfies both, so each mound is a legal exit from the other.

forceload add -128 -128 127 127

say SOAK-CHECK empty-world
moleverse colony list

# Plain mound west, shored-up mound east, the mole in the middle.
setblock -14 -3 0 moleverse:mole_mound
setblock 14 -3 0 moleverse:prepared_mole_mound
say SOAK-MARK mounds-placed

summon moleverse:mole 0 -2 0
say SOAK-MARK setup-done

tick sprint 72000
@wait Sprint completed
say SOAK-MARK finished
moleverse colony list
moleverse colony links
